{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>But on the tenth of the seventh month.</b> Even though on the other sacred assemblies it is fitting to rejoice and take delight also in eating and drinking, as it says: אִכְלוּ מַשְׁמַנִּים וּשְׁתוּ מַמְתַקִּים וְשִׁלְחוּ מָנוֹת לְאֵין נָכוֹן לוֹ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ הַיּוֹם לַאֲדֹנֵינוּ (Nehemiah 8:10) — nevertheless, the tenth of the seventh month is a Day of Atonement, to confess and for a man to be embittered over his sins; it is not a day of joy and delight, but rather a day of affliction, as it says: <b>and you shall afflict your souls and you shall bring an offering</b> — and this refers to the offerings of the High Priest and the communal offerings that come for atonement."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The word וְהִקְרַבְתֶּם in the lemma and citation appears to be Sforno's own paraphrase blending elements from the Yom Kippur context rather than quoting a single verse verbatim; translated as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:36.805285270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}